# word-chunks-keep-punctuation: pins that a `word` is a longest run of
# Characters that aren't White_Space, so punctuation stays in the word it
# touches (chapter 4, Chunk kinds; ADR 0011). `word 1 of "cat, dog"` is
# "cat,". A range of words keeps the white space between them, and runs of
# white space at either end make no empty words. A tab and U+00A0 NO-BREAK
# SPACE are White_Space and divide words; a hyphen and a comma with no space
# after it don't. Fuel, allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load words
> deliver d1 to=words message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg words/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=152 alloc=128 state=96 end=return
run words/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=152 alloc=128
pumped state=idle fuel=152

> vars
vars words firstWord="cat," secondWord="dog" lastWord="dog." both="cat,  dog." joinedCount=1 hyphened="well-known" afterTab="b" afterNbsp="b"
